  "description": "Replacement of existing first-floor windows across the front elevation with new glazing installed within the existing structural openings. The works comprise the removal of existing window frames and the installation of new units of identical overall size, alignment, and arrangement, with no alteration to the dimensions or configuration of the openings.\n\nThe replacement windows provide a more consistent and open glazed appearance, improving natural light to the upper floor while maintaining the established horizontal fenestration pattern of the building. The materials and finish have been selected to complement the existing structure and ensure the development remains in keeping with the character of the surrounding high street.\n\nThe proposal also includes the installation of a fixed external canopy at first-floor level, extending across the frontage of the commercial unit and positioned above both the entrance and the window line. The canopy comprises a lightweight framed structure with a fabric covering, projecting outward to provide weather protection and solar shading for the upper-floor accommodation.\n\nThe canopy has been designed to be proportionate to the scale of the building and aligned with the existing façade, ensuring it integrates with the overall composition of the elevation.\n\nThe proposed works do not involve any structural alterations, no change of use, and no increase in the building’s height, footprint, or overall scale. The development is considered to enhance the functionality and appearance of the premises while remaining appropriate to the character of the local streetscape.",
